    "text": "Based on the provided synthetic Python module, here is a detailed technical review and explanation.\n\n### 1. Structural Overview and Pattern Recognition\n\nThe module consists of a series of functions named `task_00000` through `task_00888` (the list appears truncated at `task_00888`, but the pattern implies a larger set). Each function follows a strict, deterministic signature: `def task_XXXXX(value: int) -> int`.\n\nThe core logic within every function is identical in structure, differing only by specific integer constants. The formula is:\n\n$$ f(value) = (value \\times A + B) \\pmod{100003} $$\n\nWhere:\n*   $A$ is the multiplier.\n*   $B$ is the additive constant.\n*   $100003$ is the modulus.\n\n### 2. Analysis of the Constants ($A$ and $B$)\n\nThe most interesting aspect of this code is how the constants $A$ and $B$ are derived.\n\n**The Additive Constant ($B$):**\nIn every function, $B$ is exactly equal to the integer part of the function"
